## Overview

### What Are Copilot Instructions?

GitHub Copilot instructions are Markdown files that guide AI-assisted development by:
- Defining coding standards and conventions
- Providing framework-specific patterns
- Preventing unwanted suggestions (e.g., framework changes)
- Ensuring consistency across the team
- Accelerating onboarding for new team members

### Instruction Hierarchy

```
.github/
├── copilot-instructions.md          # Root-level, applies to entire repository
├── AGENTS.md                         # Copilot Coding Agent configurations
└── instructions/                     # Domain-specific instructions
    ├── ui-testing.instructions.md    # UI test development
    ├── api-testing.instructions.md   # API test development
    └── ci-cd.instructions.md         # CI/CD integration
```

#### File Purpose and Scope

| File | Scope | When Applied |
|------|-------|--------------|
| `copilot-instructions.md` | Framework-wide principles | All coding activities |
| `ui-testing.instructions.md` | UI test development | Working in `features/ui/`, `core/pages/` |
| `api-testing.instructions.md` | API test development | Working in `features/api/`, `core/api/` |
| `ci-cd.instructions.md` | Pipeline configuration | Working with YAML, Docker, pipeline files |
| `AGENTS.md` | Specialized agents | When using Copilot Coding Agent feature |

